1
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:12,700
We hold these truths to be self-evident that all men are created equal, that they are endowed

2
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:17,580
by the Creator with certain unalienable rights, that among these are life, liberty, and the

3
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,740
pursuit of happiness.

4
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:27,100
Come alas any person, Jew or Gentile, for either professing doctrine is to persecute

5
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:32,740
him and such a person, whether his doctrine or practice be true or false, suffers persecution

6
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:38,010
for conscience.

7
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:42,810
Now, in view of this entire disfranchisement of one half the people of this country

8
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:47,850
and because women do feel themselves aggrieved, oppressed, and fraudulently deprived of their

9
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:53,410
most sacred rights, we insist that they have immediate mission to all the rights and privileges

10
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:59,710
which belong to them as citizens of these United States.

11
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:04,430
Are the great principles of political freedom and of natural justice embodied in that declaration

12
00:01:04,430 --> 00:01:06,830
of independence extended to us?

13
00:01:06,830 --> 00:01:12,200
What to the American slave is your Fourth of July?

14
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:16,040
Yes, we have fought for America with all her imperfections.

15
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:21,120
Not so much for what she is, but for what we know she can be.

16
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:26,000
The Negro has been here in America since 1619, a total of 344 years.

17
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,360
He is not going anywhere else.

18
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,360
This country is his home.

19
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:34,320
He wants to do his part to help make his city, state, and nation a better place for

20
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:39,040
everyone regardless of color and race.

21
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:42,880
I still have a dream, a dream deeply rooted in the American dream.

22
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:47,000
One day this nation will rise up and live out the true meaning of its creed.

23
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,080
We hold these truths to be self-evident that all men are created equal.

24
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:56,160
We have talked long enough in this country about equal rights.

25
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:58,160
We have talked for 100 years or more.

26
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:02,160
It is time now to write the next chapter and write it in the books of law.

